Dunbrack 2010 backbone-dependent rotamer library
================================================

`germinal/filters/dun2010bbdep.bin` (13,763,520 bytes) is the Dunbrack 2010
backbone-dependent rotamer library. FASPR reads it, requires it to sit beside
the executable, and hard-codes the filename, so it travels with the binary.

How it reached this repository
------------------------------
FASPR repository -> FreeBindCraft `functions/` -> `germinal/filters/`. The
search order in our own code still names `functions/FASPR`, a directory that
does not exist in this tree, which is the direct trace of that lineage.

Terms: two official statements that disagree
--------------------------------------------
  * The Dunbrack lab download page states the 2010 library is "available only
    after you have applied for a 2010 library license and approved".
  * Other sources describe the 2010 library as CC BY.

Both statements are second-hand to us, and we have not established which one
governs the copy in this repository. Whether our copy arrived through the FASPR
repository (which ships it) or directly from the lab is likewise unsettled; a
sha256 comparison against FASPR's copy would settle it and has not been done.

Why this notice exists anyway
-----------------------------
Attribution is required under the CC BY reading and harmless under the other,
so it is given rather than adjudicated. We acknowledge the Dunbrack laboratory
as the source of this rotamer library. Anyone redistributing OpenGerminal
should keep this notice with the file.
